    "summary": "Epic Dark Star > Eyes > China Doll and rare '73 Bertha shine",
    "blurb": "The second set delivers an extended Dark Star → Eyes Of The World → China Doll suite that defines the night. Jerry’s tone on Dark Star is flawless, while Keith adds tasteful accents and Bill Kreutzmann drives the improvisations. A rare early‑'73 version of Bertha rounds out a solid show.",
    "review": "Portland Memorial Coliseum, June 24 1973 – The first set wanders a bit with the usual mix of classics and a few lyrical slips, but it’s the second set that lifts this concert into the upper‑echelon of ’73 shows. A monster Dark Star launches into an inspired Eyes Of The World and then seamlessly segues into China Doll, creating one of the most memorable suites of the spring tour. Jerry Garcia’s guitar tone on Dark Star is described as “perfect,” soaring above a jazzy, percolating bass vamp from Phil Lesh that underpins the whole journey. Keith’s keyboard work adds tasteful “spiked coffee” accents toward the climax, and Bill Kreutzmann is hailed as a “freaking genius,” laying down percolating rhythms that keep the improvisations alive. The set also gifts fans a rare early‑'73 rendition of Bertha, plus strong performances of Stella Blue and Sugar Magnolia to close out the night.",
